Alicia: AtlasBank POC stuck. Rust SDK streaming failing behind their corporate TLS inspection. They also need a concrete example of function/tool calling that emits strict JSON for payments, and a pricing sketch for bursty traffic. Can someone pick this up?

Sam: Happy to own. Which environment is the POC on?

Alicia: Hosted. They may move to Dedicated after validation.

Leo: Short notes on the Rust problem: many Rust TLS stacks reject MITM certs by default. Two safe options: 1) ask Atlas infra to exempt api.redwood.ai from inspection (IP allowlist), 2) provide them a CA bundle path for the SDK to trust temporarily (only for POC). I can ship a tiny patch to the SDK that accepts a `CUSTOM_CA_PATH` env var for the POC.

Leo: Minimal websocket/SSE streaming snippet (tokio + tungstenite):

```
use tokio_tungstenite::connect_async;
use futures_util::StreamExt;

async fn sse_stream(key: &str) -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
  let url = "wss://api.redwood.ai/v1/stream?model=rl-micro&format=sse";
  let (mut ws, _) = connect_async(url).await?;
  ws.send(Message::Text(format!("{\"prompt\":\"charge $12.50 to acct-42\"}"))).await?;
  while let Some(msg) = ws.next().await { println!("part: {}", msg?); }
  Ok(())
}
```

Leo: For tool-calls use `response_format: \"func-json\"`. Example model output to call a payment tool: `{"tool":"create_charge","args":{"amount_cents":1250,"currency":"USD","payee":"acct-42","trace_id":"atlas-2026-03-21-ABC"}}`. Validate with serde/schema before invoking the payment service.

Jordan: Proxy gotcha: their proxy drops idle websockets after 30s. Recommend app-level pings every 15s and reconnect with exponential backoff. If allowlist isn't possible, we can provision a short-lived mTLS client cert for the POC (works on Hosted but requires a one-time setup).

Nina: Security summary: Hosted uses AWS KMS (HSM-backed). We support BYOK and on-prem HSM for Dedicated/Private. SOC2 Type II and SAML/OIDC supported. I'll DM the SOC2 package link and the SSO config doc.

Kevin: Pricing quick sketch: for bursty 1k TPS with ~150 tokens per request, hosted bursts estimate $18k-$32k/month depending on caching. Dedicated steady 1k TPS with SLA ~ $55k-$85k/month. I'll prepare two sample spreadsheets.

infra-bot: Provisioned staging sandbox `atlas-poc-staging-03` with API key `REDS_TEST_03` (expires 24h).

Alicia: Thanks. Action items: Leo to post SDK patch + CA guidance, Jordan to list egress IPs + mTLS instructions, Nina to share security packet, Kevin to send cost spreadsheets. Sam and I will join the sync tomorrow.

Sam: I'll be on the call.

